## Challenges

One of the primary challenges during this investigation was working with multiple log formats, each containing different timestamp structures and event types. Selecting the appropriate Linux commands and filtering techniques was important to isolate relevant information while minimizing unnecessary output. This project reinforced the value of combining multiple command-line utilities to efficiently analyze large log files.

## Key Takeaways

This project strengthened my ability to analyze Linux log files using native command-line tools and identify meaningful security events from large datasets. It also improved my understanding of authentication logs, web server activity, and system events while reinforcing the importance of efficient log analysis during digital forensic investigations.
